      "source": [
        "## Generate BoW DataFrame\n",
        "\n",
        "### Subtask:\n",
        "Create a Bag of Words (BoW) representation of the preprocessed headlines and convert it into a structured pandas DataFrame.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "520f5175"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will import the CountVectorizer from scikit-learn, transform the cleaned headlines into a Bag of Words representation, and then create a new DataFrame to store and display these word counts.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 192
        },
        "id": "6ab98583",
        "outputId": "3c7fda3f-f204-461a-ffd0-fb093101293e"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer\n",
        "\n",
        "# Instantiate CountVectorizer with English stop words\n",
        "vectorizer = CountVectorizer(stop_words='english')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit and transform the preprocessed headlines\n",
        "bow_matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(df_new_headlines['Cleaned_Headline'])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Retrieve feature names (words)\n",
        "feature_names = vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create a DataFrame representing the Bag of Words\n",
        "df_new_bow = pd.DataFrame(bow_matrix.toarray(), columns=feature_names)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the BoW DataFrame\n",
        "print('Bag of Words (BoW) DataFrame:')\n",
        "df_new_bow"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Bag of Words (BoW) DataFrame:\n"
          ]
        },
