    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ae9fa63c"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Apply LDA Modeling\n",
        "\n",
        "### Subtask:\n",
        "Initialize and fit a Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) model to discover the latent topics in the new dataset.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "53d7224d"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will import the LatentDirichletAllocation class, instantiate the model with 2 topics, fit it to the BoW matrix, and then transform the matrix to obtain the topic distributions for each headline.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "4fa64fef",
        "outputId": "b31dc1d0-d8a9-4763-e225-d5798d76507d"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.decomposition import LatentDirichletAllocation\n",
        "\n",
        "# Instantiate the LDA model with 2 topics\n",
        "lda_model = LatentDirichletAllocation(n_components=2, random_state=4)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit the model using the previously generated bow_matrix\n",
        "lda_model.fit(bow_matrix)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Transform the bow_matrix to get topic distributions for each headline\n",
        "lda_output = lda_model.transform(bow_matrix)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Print the shape of the output to verify\n",
        "print('LDA Output Shape:', lda_output.shape)\n",
        "print('LDA Output (Topic Distributions):')\n",
        "print(lda_output)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "LDA Output Shape: (4, 2)\n",
            "LDA Output (Topic Distributions):\n",
            "[[0.11177908 0.88822092]\n",
            " [0.13006409 0.86993591]\n",
            " [0.88532706 0.11467294]\n",
            " [0.89528147 0.10471853]]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "612c36bc"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Identify Topic Keywords\n",
        "\n",
        "### Subtask:\n",
        "Extract and display the top words associated with each discovered topic to understand the themes.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1b8da909"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will extract the top 5 keywords for each topic by accessing the `components_` of the LDA model, sorting them to find the highest weights, and mapping those indices back to the feature names.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "1a7ac9a6",
        "outputId": "6de22724-7c6c-45f0-e3aa-4cc8c110c9a6"
      },
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Function to display the top keywords for each topic\n",
        "def display_topics(model, feature_names, no_top_words):\n",
        "    for topic_idx, topic in enumerate(model.components_):\n",
        "        # Get indices of the top words by weight and reverse the order\n",
        "        top_indices = topic.argsort()[::-1][:no_top_words]\n",
        "        # Map indices to words\n",
        "        top_words = [feature_names[i] for i in top_indices]\n",
        "        print(f'Topic {topic_idx}: {\", \".join(top_words)}')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display top 5 words for each topic\n",
        "print('Top 5 Keywords for Each Topic:')\n",
        "display_topics(lda_model, feature_names, 5)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Top 5 Keywords for Each Topic:\n",
            "Topic 0: congress, government, state, form, bumra\n",
            "Topic 1: match, century, virat, scored, won\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "738e7cb3"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Assign Topics to Headlines\n",
        "\n",
        "### Subtask:\n",
        "Map the dominant topic back to each original headline in the DataFrame.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9b85091c"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will determine the dominant topic for each headline by finding the index of the maximum probability in the LDA output and then add this information as a new column to the headlines DataFrame.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 192
        },
        "id": "bf40056c",
        "outputId": "3841dbaf-beb4-4408-9dcf-8c6110bdbe53"
      },
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Determine the dominant topic for each headline using argmax on the LDA output\n",
        "dominant_topics = np.argmax(lda_output, axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add a new column 'Topic' to the df_new_headlines DataFrame\n",
        "df_new_headlines['Topic'] = dominant_topics\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the updated DataFrame to verify the topic assignment\n",
        "print('Updated Headlines with Assigned Topics:')\n",
        "df_new_headlines"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
