        "id": "5b2da22c"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Task\n",
        "Perform topic modeling on the news headlines using Non-Negative Matrix Factorization (NMF). First, preprocess the text by tokenizing, removing stopwords, and applying lemmatization using NLTK, ensuring that the \"punkt\", \"punkt_tab\", \"stopwords\", and \"wordnet\" datasets are downloaded. Next, generate a Bag of Words (BoW) representation of the lemmatized headlines. Then, fit an NMF model to the BoW matrix to discover latent topics. Finally, analyze the top keywords for each topic, assign the most relevant topic to each original headline, and provide a summary of the findings and insights."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ab10674a"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Preprocess Headlines with Lemmatization (Retry)\n",
        "\n",
        "### Subtask:\n",
        "Clean the headlines, tokenize, remove stopwords, and apply lemmatization using NLTK to prepare the corpus, ensuring all required datasets are available.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c020a6a0"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will import the necessary NLTK components, download the required datasets (including 'punkt_tab' to resolve the previous error), and then define and apply a preprocessing function to lemmatize the headlines in the DataFrame.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 362
        },
        "id": "8a2181cc",
        "outputId": "d37c09f7-4a31-45e4-e5a4-2e65a8bceb45"
      },
      "source": [
        "import nltk\n",
        "from nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize\n",
        "from nltk.corpus import stopwords\n",
        "from nltk.stem import WordNetLemmatizer\n",
        "\n",
        "# Download necessary NLTK resource packages, including 'punkt_tab'\n",
        "nltk.download('punkt')\n",
        "nltk.download('punkt_tab')\n",
        "nltk.download('stopwords')\n",
        "nltk.download('wordnet')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize lemmatizer and stop words\n",
        "lemmatizer = WordNetLemmatizer()\n",
        "stop_words = set(stopwords.words('english'))\n",
        "\n",
        "def preprocess_lemmatize(text):\n",
        "    # Tokenize and convert to lowercase\n",
        "    tokens = word_tokenize(text.lower())\n",
        "    # Remove non-alphabetic tokens and stop words, then lemmatize\n",
        "    lemmatized = [lemmatizer.lemmatize(w) for w in tokens if w.isalpha() and w not in stop_words]\n",
        "    return ' '.join(lemmatized)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply the preprocessing function to create the 'Lemmatized_Headline' column\n",
        "df_new_headlines['Lemmatized_Headline'] = df_new_headlines['Headline'].apply(preprocess_lemmatize)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the head of the DataFrame to verify the transformation\n",
        "print('DataFrame with Lemmatized Headlines:')\n",
        "df_new_headlines[['Headline', 'Lemmatized_Headline']].head()"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stderr",
