    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c5db3dc5"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will import the NMF class, instantiate the model with 2 topics, fit it to the BoW matrix generated from lemmatized headlines, and then transform the matrix to obtain the topic weights for each headline.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ac516d26",
        "outputId": "3ca23234-57f4-4cdb-bc60-dec5677dc976"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.decomposition import NMF\n",
        "\n",
        "# Instantiate the NMF model with 2 topics\n",
        "nmf_model = NMF(n_components=2, random_state=42, init='nndsvd')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit the model using the lemmatized BoW matrix\n",
        "nmf_model.fit(bow_matrix_nmf)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Transform the matrix to get topic distributions for each headline\n",
        "nmf_output = nmf_model.transform(bow_matrix_nmf)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Print the shape of the output and the topic distributions\n",
        "print('NMF Output Shape:', nmf_output.shape)\n",
        "print('NMF Output (Topic Distributions):')\n",
        "print(nmf_output)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "NMF Output Shape: (6, 2)\n",
            "NMF Output (Topic Distributions):\n",
            "[[1.14893357 0.        ]\n",
            " [0.         0.        ]\n",
            " [1.14893357 0.        ]\n",
            " [0.         0.        ]\n",
            " [0.51643385 0.        ]\n",
            " [0.         1.41421597]]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f40d74ad"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will extract the top 5 keywords for each topic from the NMF model using the feature names from the NMF vectorizer and then assign the dominant topic to each headline by finding the index of the maximum weight in the NMF output matrix.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 324
        },
        "id": "2bbdd00a",
        "outputId": "c9125525-8231-43b0-b3e8-bd783538094c"
      },
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Get the feature names from the NMF vectorizer\n",
        "feature_names_nmf = vectorizer_nmf.get_feature_names_out()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Function to display the top keywords for each topic in the NMF model\n",
        "def display_nmf_topics(model, feature_names, no_top_words):\n",
        "    for topic_idx, topic in enumerate(model.components_):\n",
        "        # Get the indices of the highest-weighted words\n",
        "        top_indices = topic.argsort()[::-1][:no_top_words]\n",
        "        top_words = [feature_names[i] for i in top_indices]\n",
        "        print(f'Topic {topic_idx}: {\", \".join(top_words)}')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display top 5 keywords for each topic discovered by NMF\n",
        "print('Top 5 Keywords for NMF Topics:')\n",
        "display_nmf_topics(nmf_model, feature_names_nmf, 5)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Determine the dominant topic for each headline from the NMF output\n",
        "# We use argmax to find the index of the highest probability/weight\n",
        "dominant_nmf_topics = np.argmax(nmf_output, axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add the NMF topic assignment to the original DataFrame\n",
        "df_new_headlines['NMF_Topic'] = dominant_nmf_topics\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the DataFrame to verify the topic assignments\n",
        "print('\\nUpdated Headlines with NMF Topic Assignments:')\n",
        "df_new_headlines[['Headline', 'Lemmatized_Headline', 'NMF_Topic']]"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
